        {
            "id": "751bd5b7-30f6-4c9a-b9a8-b19a4d5b43c0",
            "build_id": "bd9f5a33-6e5e-4f44-b981-8c074c2214f6",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-07T11:05:15.674154+00:00",
            "notes": "[Cyclone](item_197843aa-de82-4387-b6c9-e5e1549b4832) works well for easy extra dps. Any power here can work well, honestly. [Mighty Gust](item_e9309cc7-c02b-47ad-b953-37510d3d2768) can be ok if they are constantly running you down. Pick what feels comfortable.\n\n[Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98), [Mark of the Kitsune](item_09a53e39-25aa-4f66-ba51-bedbc543a1eb) and [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6) are usually the most universally good choices here. Take Multi tool or charged plating instead of one of the non core epics if you are poor.\n\nAll the previously mentioned options from last round are still up for grabs here. You can take [Champion's Kit](item_8682f8c7-8811-439b-8d50-fa81cd43ddce) over Nano cola or a non core epic if you are mega rich.\n\nYou will have a LOT of bola damage at this point, and can pretty easily 100 to 0 most squishies with your Lillie into right click combo. If you see someone in a tight space or a few of them grouped together, throw out your Lillie shot as the AoE burn damage can easily chunk for half health or more even without any impact damage. if you can direct impact a squishy with a Lillie shot and they are around half heath, they with likely either die or need to have their team invest cooldowns to save them.\n\nDont sleep on your weapon damage either, as [Three-tap Tommygun](item_39c5d2a4-1db0-444f-86d9-2a1e9a331429) and [Mark of the Kitsune](item_09a53e39-25aa-4f66-ba51-bedbc543a1eb) will now provide a ton of extra weapon dps. You will also be able to melt tanks quite quickly.\n\nTreat your ult with much more respect that you would normally. It can easily one shot entire groups of squishies now, as long as they aren't building a lot of tanky items. Use mini bola first for easy ult connections. Dont be afraid to use ult on the tank if you get a decent chance, as it can easily catch them off guard and quickly burst them before they can react.",
